# Copy to .env and adjust. SQLite keeps the zero-config local story:
#   npm install && cp .env.example .env
#   npm run db:push && npm run db:seed && npm run dev
# The path is resolved relative to prisma/schema.prisma.

# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default (zero-config local dev). The `db/` folder lives at the
# repo root, git-ignored. A RELATIVE `file:` URL is resolved against
# prisma/schema.prisma — exactly like the Prisma CLI — so `file:../db/custom.db`
# points at <repo>/db/custom.db for the CLI (db:push/db:seed), `next build`,
# and the running server alike, regardless of the process working directory.
# (src/lib/db-path.ts implements this resolution; tests/db-path.test.ts
# pins the contract. The npm scripts pin this URL inline so a stray
# parent-directory .env or exported shell var can never hijack it.)
# For production, an ABSOLUTE path is still recommended — see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4.
#
# To use PostgreSQL instead:
#   1. Set provider = "postgresql" in prisma/schema.prisma
#   2. Set DATABASE_URL to a PostgreSQL connection string
#   3. npm run db:push && npm run db:seed
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"
# PostgreSQL example:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/app_db

# ---- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical public origin. Load-bearing: src/lib/auth.ts's cookieSecureFlag()
# sets the session cookie's Secure flag only for https:// origins, so an
# HTTP preview (localhost, `next start` behind plain HTTP) keeps working
# login sessions. Set to the deployed URL in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Session signing secret for HMAC cookie auth.
# REQUIRED in production: generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Falls back to an insecure dev-only constant when unset.
AUTH_SECRET=""

# ---- Maps --------------------------------------------------------------------
# CARTO Basemaps API key (session-63). The provider deprecated anonymous
# raster-tile access — keyless basemaps.cartocdn.com URLs return an
# "API KEY REQUIRED" watermark placeholder. src/lib/carto.ts appends this
# key as the ?key= param on every tile URL (the home route map's
# light_nolabels grid + the /map light_nolabels basemap). UNSET is fine: the
# committed default (docs/carto_key.txt) applies, so keyless-env builds
# still get clean tiles. Set only to switch accounts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CARTO_KEY=cb1_465p_1_988c53d611811b5d4bdb6b32

# ---- Debug ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: set DEBUG_DBPATH=1 to print every db-path anchor candidate and
# schema check to the server log (the first stop for SQLite "Error code 14").
# DEBUG_DBPATH=1
